Add a hidden opt-in option `--resolution-cache DIR`, which requires `--type-system-refresh`. It stores each module's resolution result in DIR, keyed by the module's own source, its options, the producer, and the result structures of its prerequisites. A later run reuses each module whose key is unchanged instead of resolving it. An edit that leaves a module's result alike, such as a comment, does not re-resolve the modules that depend on it. `--resolution-cache-check` also resolves every reused module afresh and reports an error if the two results differ. Modules whose results cannot be stored resolve normally, and without the option resolution is unchanged.
